commit ec5b8c4d5c412a57f3e8a7f8e70d669a10cb7f60
Author: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 19:19:31 2026 -0800

    fix(core): project single literals, mixed booleans and @ignore the way Storybook reads them

    A single string or number literal was written as a bare type name, so
    Storybook picked an object control; it is now a one-option enum. A boolean
    in a mixed literal union was written as the option string "true"; it now
    stays a type name, which Storybook's converter parses into real options.
    A prop tagged @ignore no longer appears in the RDT-shaped output, as in
    Storybook's own docgen. The canonical output is unchanged.

    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ
